IMPORT prelude

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 (NSW) -- the dates, in one small module. It uses only the built-in date functions
-- (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), FLOOR and MODULO, not the daydate
-- library, and defines no YMD.
--
-- READINGS (forks F1 and F2 in NOTES.md): a period of months "after" a day ends on the same day of the month that many
-- months later (the day itself is not counted), or on that month's last day where the month is shorter (31 August
-- plus 6 months is 28 or 29 February). A period of days "after" a day does not count that day. A working day is a day
-- that is not a Saturday or Sunday; public and bank holidays are an input (s 94B(2)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2024). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- Fork F1: the same day of the month n months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- The built-in serial makes 1 January 1900 (a Monday) a number that leaves 1 when divided by 7: so 0 is a Sunday and
-- 6 a Saturday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a weekday` `the day` IF
    (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) AT LEAST 1 AND (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) AT MOST 5

-- The n-th day after a day that is a Monday to Friday (the day itself is not counted).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the weekday number` n `after` `the day` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `it is a weekday` (`the day` `plus days` 1)
         THEN `the weekday number` (n MINUS 1) `after` (`the day` `plus days` 1)
         ELSE `the weekday number` n `after` (`the day` `plus days` 1)
